  "goodToKnow": "Der Maurer (die Maurerin) is a bricklayer or mason, one of the classic German Ausbildungsberufe (trades learned through an apprenticeship). Pünktlich wie die Maurer is a joke about knocking off exactly on time. Die Mauer is a wall, and in German history die Mauer means the Berlin Wall (1961–1989). Mauern means to build walls and, in football, to defend with everyone back. Freemasons are die Freimaurer."
